#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Repetition codes {#repetition-codes}"
msgstr "Kod ulangan {#repetition-codes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll begin the lesson with a discussion of *repetition codes.*\n"
"Repetition codes don't protect quantum information against every type of error that can occur on qubits, but they do form the basis for the 9-qubit Shor code, which we'll see in the next lesson, and they're also useful for explaining the basics of error correction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan memulakan pelajaran dengan perbincangan tentang *kod ulangan.*\n"
"Kod ulangan tidak melindungi maklumat kuantum daripada setiap jenis ralat yang boleh berlaku pada qubit, tetapi ia membentuk asas kepada kod Shor 9-Qubit, yang akan kita lihat dalam pelajaran seterusnya, dan ia juga berguna untuk menerangkan asas-asas pembetulan ralat.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical encoding and decoding {#classical-encoding-and-decoding}"
msgstr "Pengekodan dan penyahkodan klasik {#classical-encoding-and-decoding}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Repetition codes are extremely basic examples of error correcting codes.\n"
"The idea is that we can protect bits against errors by simply repeating each bit some fixed number of times.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod ulangan adalah contoh paling asas bagi kod pembetulan ralat.\n"
"Ideanya ialah kita boleh melindungi bit daripada ralat dengan hanya mengulang setiap bit beberapa kali tetap.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, let's first consider the 3-bit repetition code, just in the context of classical information to start.\n"
"This code encodes one bit into three by repeating the bit three times, so $0$ is encoded as $000$ and $1$ is encoded as $111.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Khususnya, marilah kita pertimbangkan dahulu kod ulangan 3-bit, hanya dalam konteks maklumat klasik untuk bermula.\n"
"Kod ini mengekodkan satu bit ke dalam tiga dengan mengulang bit tiga kali, jadi $0$ dikodkan sebagai $000$ dan $1$ dikodkan sebagai $111.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"0 & \\mapsto 000\\\\\n"
"1 & \\mapsto 111\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"0 & \\mapsto 000\\\\\n"
"1 & \\mapsto 111\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If nothing goes wrong, we can obviously distinguish the two possibilities for the original bit from their encodings.\n"
"The point is that if there was an error and one of the three bits flipped, meaning that a 0 changes into a 1 or a 1 changes to a 0, then we can still figure out what the original bit was by determining which of the two binary values appears twice.\n"
"Equivalently, we can *decode* by computing the majority value (that is, the binary value that appears most frequently).\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika tiada yang berlaku, kita jelas boleh membezakan dua kemungkinan untuk bit asal daripada pengekodan mereka.\n"
"Perkara yang penting ialah jika ada ralat dan salah satu daripada tiga bit terbalik, bermakna 0 bertukar menjadi 1 atau 1 bertukar menjadi 0, kita masih boleh mengetahui apa bit asal dengan menentukan nilai binari mana yang muncul dua kali.\n"
"Secara setara, kita boleh *menyahkodkan* dengan mengira nilai majoriti (iaitu nilai binari yang paling kerap muncul).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"a b c \\mapsto \\operatorname{majority}(a,b,c)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"a b c \\mapsto \\operatorname{majority}(a,b,c)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, if 2 or 3 bits of the encoding flip, then the decoding won't work properly and the wrong bit will be recovered, but if at most 1 of the 3 bits flip, the decoding will be correct.\n"
"This is a typical property of error correcting codes in general: they may allow for the correction of errors, but only if there aren't too many of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudah tentu, jika 2 atau 3 bit pengekodan terbalik, maka penyahkodan tidak akan berfungsi dengan betul dan bit yang salah akan dipulihkan, tetapi jika paling banyak 1 daripada 3 bit terbalik, penyahkodan akan betul.\n"
"Ini adalah sifat biasa kod pembetulan ralat secara umum: ia mungkin membenarkan pembetulan ralat, tetapi hanya jika tidak terlalu banyak.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Noise reduction for the binary symmetric channel {#noise-reduction-for-the-"
"binary-symmetric-channel}"
msgstr ""
"Pengurangan hingar untuk saluran simetri binari {#noise-reduction-for-the-"
"binary-symmetric-channel}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For an example of a situation in which the chances of making an error can be decreased using a repetition code,\n"
"suppose that our goal is to communicate a single bit to a hypothetical receiver, and we're able to transmit bits through a so-called *binary symmetric channel*, which flips each bit sent through it independently with some probability $p.$\n"
"That is, with probability $1-p,$ the receiver gets whatever bit was sent through the channel, but with probability $p,$ the bit-flips and the receiver gets the opposite bit value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh situasi di mana peluang membuat ralat boleh dikurangkan menggunakan kod ulangan,\n"
"andaikan matlamat kita adalah untuk menyampaikan satu bit kepada penerima hipotetikal, dan kita boleh menghantar bit melalui saluran yang dipanggil *saluran simetri binari*, yang membalikkan setiap bit yang dihantar melaluinya secara bebas dengan kebarangkalian $p$ tertentu.\n"
"Iaitu, dengan kebarangkalian $1-p,$ penerima mendapat bit yang dihantar melalui saluran, tetapi dengan kebarangkalian $p,$ bit terbalik dan penerima mendapat nilai bit yang bertentangan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, if we choose not to use the 3-bit repetition code, and simply send whatever bit we have in mind through the channel, the receiver therefore receives the wrong bit with probability $p.$\n"
"On the other hand, if we first encode the bit we want to send using the 3-bit repetition code, and then send each of the three bits of the encoding through the channel, then each one of them flips independently with probability $p.$\n"
"The chances of a bit-flip are now greater because there are now three bits that might flip rather than one, but if at most one of the bits flips, then the receiver will decode correctly.\n"
"An error therefore persists after decoding only if two or more of the bits flip during transmission.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, jika kita memilih untuk tidak menggunakan kod ulangan 3-bit, dan hanya menghantar bit yang kita fikirkan melalui saluran, penerima oleh itu menerima bit yang salah dengan kebarangkalian $p.$\n"
"Sebaliknya, jika kita mula-mula mengekodkan bit yang ingin kita hantar menggunakan kod ulangan 3-bit, dan kemudian menghantar setiap tiga bit pengekodan melalui saluran, maka setiap satunya akan terbalik secara bebas dengan kebarangkalian $p.$\n"
"Peluang bit-flip kini lebih besar kerana kini ada tiga bit yang mungkin terbalik dan bukannya satu, tetapi jika paling banyak satu bit terbalik, maka penerima akan menyahkod dengan betul.\n"
"Oleh itu, ralat hanya kekal selepas penyahkodan jika dua atau lebih bit terbalik semasa penghantaran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probability that two bits flip during transmission is $3p^2(1-p),$ which is $p^2(1-p)$ for each of the three choices for the bit that doesn't flip, while the probability that all three bits flip is $p^3.$\n"
"The total probability of two or three bit-flips is therefore\n"
msgstr ""
"Kebarangkalian dua bit terbalik semasa penghantaran adalah $3p^2(1-p),$ iaitu $p^2(1-p)$ untuk setiap tiga pilihan bit yang tidak terbalik, manakala kebarangkalian ketiga-tiga bit terbalik adalah $p^3.$\n"
"Jumlah kebarangkalian dua atau tiga bit-flip adalah oleh itu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"3 p^2 (1 - p) + p^3 = 3 p^2 - 2 p^3.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"3 p^2 (1 - p) + p^3 = 3 p^2 - 2 p^3.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For values of $p$ smaller than one-half, this results in a decrease in the probability that the receiver ends up with the wrong bit.\n"
"There will still be a chance of an error in this case, but the code *decreases* the likelihood.\n"
"(For values of $p$ *greater* than one-half, on the other hand, the code actually *increases* the likelihood that the receiver gets the wrong bit.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk nilai $p$ yang lebih kecil daripada satu perdua, ini menghasilkan penurunan dalam kebarangkalian bahawa penerima akhirnya mendapat bit yang salah.\n"
"Masih akan ada peluang ralat dalam kes ini, tetapi kod itu *mengurangkan* kemungkinannya.\n"
"(Untuk nilai $p$ yang *lebih besar* daripada satu perdua, sebaliknya, kod itu sebenarnya *meningkatkan* kemungkinan bahawa penerima mendapat bit yang salah.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Error probability graph for the 3 bit repetition code for a binary "
"symmetric channel](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/binary-symmetric-error.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Graf kebarangkalian ralat untuk kod ulangan 3-bit bagi saluran simetri "
"binari](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/binary-symmetric-error.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding qubits {#encoding-qubits}"
msgstr "Pengekodan qubit {#encoding-qubits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 3-bit repetition code is a classical error correcting code, but we can consider what happens if we try to use it to protect *qubits* against errors.\n"
"As we'll see, it's not a very impressive quantum error correcting code, because it actually makes some errors more likely.\n"
"It is, however, the first step toward the Shor code, and will serve us well from a pedagogical viewpoint.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod ulangan 3-bit adalah kod pembetulan ralat klasik, tetapi kita boleh mempertimbangkan apa yang berlaku jika kita cuba menggunakannya untuk melindungi *qubit* daripada ralat.\n"
"Seperti yang akan kita lihat, ia bukan kod pembetulan ralat kuantum yang sangat bagus, kerana ia sebenarnya menjadikan beberapa ralat lebih berkemungkinan.\n"
"Walau bagaimanapun, ia adalah langkah pertama ke arah kod Shor, dan akan berguna dari sudut pedagogi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, when we refer to the 3-bit repetition code being used for "
"qubits, we have in mind an encoding of a qubit where *standard basis states*"
" are repeated three times, so that a single-qubit state vector is encoded as"
" follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk jelaskan, apabila kita merujuk kepada kod ulangan 3-bit yang digunakan"
" untuk qubit, kita membayangkan pengekodan qubit di mana *keadaan asas "
"piawai* diulang tiga kali, supaya vektor keadaan satu-Qubit dikodkan seperti"
" berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle \\mapsto \\alpha \\vert 000\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle \\mapsto \\alpha \\vert 000\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This encoding is easily implemented by the following quantum circuit, which "
"makes use of two initialized workspace qubits and two controlled-NOT "
"gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengekodan ini mudah dilaksanakan oleh Circuit kuantum berikut, yang "
"menggunakan dua qubit ruang kerja yang diinialisasi dan dua gate controlled-"
"NOT.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Encoding circuit for the 3-bit repetition "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-encoder.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit pengekodan untuk kod ulangan "
"3-bit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-encoder.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice, in particular, that this encoding is not the same as repeating the quantum state three times, as in a given qubit state vector being encoded as $\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\mapsto \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Such an encoding cannot be implemented for an unknown quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ by the no cloning theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan, khususnya, bahawa pengekodan ini tidak sama dengan mengulang keadaan kuantum tiga kali, seperti vektor keadaan qubit tertentu yang dikodkan sebagai $\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\mapsto \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Pengekodan sedemikian tidak boleh dilaksanakan untuk keadaan kuantum yang tidak diketahui $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ oleh teorem tiada-pengklonan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bit-flip errors {#bit-flip-errors}"
msgstr "Ralat bit-flip {#bit-flip-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now suppose that an error takes place after the encoding has been performed.\n"
"Specifically, let's suppose that an $X$ gate, or in other words a bit-flip, occurs on one of the qubits.\n"
"For instance, if the middle qubit experiences a bit-flip, the state of the three qubits is transformed into this state:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang andaikan bahawa ralat berlaku selepas pengekodan dilakukan.\n"
"Khususnya, marilah kita andaikan bahawa gate $X$, atau dengan kata lain bit-flip, berlaku pada salah satu qubit.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, jika qubit tengah mengalami bit-flip, keadaan tiga qubit diubah menjadi keadaan ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert 010\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 101\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert 010\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 101\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, this isn't the only sort of error that could occur — and it's also reasonable to question the assumption that an error takes the form of a perfect, unitary operation.\n"
"We'll return to these issues in the last section of the lesson, and for now we can view an error of this form as being just one possible type of error (albeit a fundamentally important one).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudah tentu, ini bukan satu-satunya jenis ralat yang boleh berlaku — dan ia juga wajar mempersoalkan andaian bahawa ralat mengambil bentuk operasi unitari yang sempurna.\n"
"Kita akan kembali kepada isu-isu ini dalam bahagian terakhir pelajaran, dan buat masa ini kita boleh melihat ralat dalam bentuk ini sebagai hanya satu jenis ralat yang mungkin (walaupun yang paling penting secara asas).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can see clearly from the mathematical expression for the state above that the middle bit is the one that's different inside of each ket.\n"
"But suppose that we had the three qubits in our possession and didn't know their state.\n"
"If we suspected that a bit-flip may have occurred, one option to verify that a bit flipped would be to perform a standard basis measurement, which, in the case at hand, would cause us to see $010$ or $101$ with probabilities $\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2$ and $\\vert\\beta\\vert^2,$ respectively.\n"
"In either case, our conclusion would be that the middle bit flipped — but, unfortunately, we would lose the original quantum state $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"This is the state we're trying to protect, so measuring in the standard basis is an unsatisfactory option.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh melihat dengan jelas daripada ungkapan matematik untuk keadaan di atas bahawa bit tengah adalah yang berbeza di dalam setiap ket.\n"
"Tetapi andaikan kita mempunyai tiga qubit dalam pegangan kita dan tidak mengetahui keadaannya.\n"
"Jika kita mengesyaki bahawa bit-flip mungkin telah berlaku, satu pilihan untuk mengesahkan bahawa bit terbalik ialah melakukan pengukuran asas piawai, yang, dalam kes yang dihadapi, akan menyebabkan kita melihat $010$ atau $101$ dengan kebarangkalian $\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2$ dan $\\vert\\beta\\vert^2,$ masing-masing.\n"
"Dalam mana-mana kes, kesimpulan kita ialah bit tengah terbalik — tetapi, sayangnya, kita akan kehilangan keadaan kuantum asal $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Inilah keadaan yang kita cuba lindungi, jadi mengukur dalam asas piawai adalah pilihan yang tidak memuaskan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What we can do instead is to use the following quantum circuit, feeding the encoded state into the top three qubits.\n"
"This circuit nondestructively measures the *parity* of the standard basis states of the top two qubits as well as the bottom two qubits of the three-qubit encoding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang boleh kita lakukan sebaliknya ialah menggunakan Circuit kuantum berikut, dengan memasukkan keadaan yang dikodkan ke dalam tiga qubit atas.\n"
"Circuit ini mengukur *pariti* keadaan asas piawai dua qubit atas serta dua qubit bawah daripada pengekodan tiga-Qubit secara tidak merosakkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Error detection circuit for the 3-bit repetition "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-error-detection.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit pengesanan ralat untuk kod ulangan "
"3-bit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-error-detection.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Under the assumption that at most one bit flipped, one can easily deduce from the measurement outcomes the location of the bit-flip (or the absence of one).\n"
"In particular, as the following four circuit diagrams illustrate, the measurement outcome $00$ indicates that no bit-flip occurred, while the three other possibilities indicate which qubit experienced a bit-flip.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan andaian bahawa paling banyak satu bit terbalik, seseorang boleh dengan mudah menyimpulkan daripada hasil pengukuran lokasi bit-flip (atau ketiadaannya).\n"
"Khususnya, seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh empat gambar rajah Circuit berikut, hasil pengukuran $00$ menunjukkan tiada bit-flip berlaku, manakala tiga kemungkinan lain menunjukkan qubit mana yang mengalami bit-flip.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Error detection for the 3-bit repetition code (no "
"errors)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-decode-no-error.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pengesanan ralat untuk kod ulangan 3-bit (tiada "
"ralat)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-decode-no-error.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Error detection for the 3-bit repetition code (error on qubit "
"0)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-decode-e0.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pengesanan ralat untuk kod ulangan 3-bit (ralat pada qubit "
"0)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-decode-e0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Error detection for the 3-bit repetition code (error on qubit "
"1)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-decode-e1.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pengesanan ralat untuk kod ulangan 3-bit (ralat pada qubit "
"1)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-decode-e1.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Error detection for the 3-bit repetition code (error on qubit "
"2)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-decode-e2.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pengesanan ralat untuk kod ulangan 3-bit (ralat pada qubit "
"2)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-decode-e2.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Crucially, the state of the top three qubits does not collapse in any of the cases, which allows us to correct a bit-flip error if one has occurred — by simply applying the same bit-flip again with an $X$ gate.\n"
"The following table summarizes the states we obtain from at most one bit-flip, the measurement outcomes (which are called the *syndrome* in the context of error correction), and the correction needed to get back to the original encoding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang penting, keadaan tiga qubit atas tidak runtuh dalam mana-mana kes, yang membolehkan kita membetulkan ralat bit-flip jika ia berlaku — dengan hanya menggunakan bit-flip yang sama lagi dengan gate $X$.\n"
"Jadual berikut meringkaskan keadaan yang kita peroleh daripada paling banyak satu bit-flip, hasil pengukuran (yang dipanggil *sindrom* dalam konteks pembetulan ralat), dan pembetulan yang diperlukan untuk kembali ke pengekodan asal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| State | Syndrome | Correction |\n"
"|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert 000\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle$ | $00$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert 001\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 110\\rangle$ | $01$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes X$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert 010\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 101\\rangle$ | $11$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes X\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert 100\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 011\\rangle$ | $10$ | $X\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Keadaan | Sindrom | Pembetulan |\n"
"|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert 000\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle$ | $00$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert 001\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 110\\rangle$ | $01$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes X$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert 010\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 101\\rangle$ | $11$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes X\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert 100\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 011\\rangle$ | $10$ | $X\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once again, we're only considering the possibility that at most one bit-flip occurred.\n"
"This wouldn't work correctly if two or three bit-flips occurred, and we also haven't considered other possible errors besides bit-flips.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekali lagi, kita hanya mempertimbangkan kemungkinan bahawa paling banyak satu bit-flip berlaku.\n"
"Ini tidak akan berfungsi dengan betul jika dua atau tiga bit-flip berlaku, dan kita juga belum mempertimbangkan ralat lain selain bit-flip.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Phase-flip errors {#phase-flip-errors}"
msgstr "Ralat phase-flip {#phase-flip-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the quantum setting, bit-flip errors aren't the only errors we need to worry about.\n"
"For instance, we also have to worry about *phase-flip errors*, which are described by $Z$ gates.\n"
"Along the same lines as bit-flip errors, we can think about phase-flip errors as representing just another possibility for an error that can affect a qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam tetapan kuantum, ralat bit-flip bukan satu-satunya ralat yang perlu kita bimbangkan.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, kita juga perlu bimbang tentang *ralat phase-flip*, yang digambarkan oleh gate $Z$.\n"
"Seiring dengan ralat bit-flip, kita boleh memikirkan ralat phase-flip sebagai mewakili hanya satu lagi kemungkinan untuk ralat yang boleh mempengaruhi sesebuah qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, as we will see in the last section of the lesson, which is on the so-called *discretization of errors* for quantum error correcting codes, a focus on bit-flip errors and phase-flip errors turns out to be well-justified.\n"
"Specifically, the ability to correct a bit-flip error, a phase-flip error, or both of these errors simultaneously automatically implies the ability to correct an arbitrary quantum error on a single qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walau bagaimanapun, seperti yang akan kita lihat dalam bahagian terakhir pelajaran, yang berkaitan dengan *pendiskretan ralat* bagi kod pembetulan ralat kuantum, fokus pada ralat bit-flip dan ralat phase-flip ternyata sangat dijustifikasi.\n"
"Khususnya, keupayaan untuk membetulkan ralat bit-flip, ralat phase-flip, atau kedua-dua ralat ini secara serentak secara automatik membawa kepada keupayaan untuk membetulkan sebarang ralat kuantum sewenang-wenang pada satu qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, the 3-bit repetition code doesn't protect against phase-flips at all.\n"
"For instance, suppose that a qubit state $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle$ has been encoded using the 3-bit repetition code, and a phase-flip error occurs on the middle qubit.\n"
"This results in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Malangnya, kod ulangan 3-bit tidak melindungi langsung terhadap phase-flip.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, andaikan keadaan qubit $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle$ telah dikodkan menggunakan kod ulangan 3-bit, dan ralat phase-flip berlaku pada qubit tengah.\n"
"Ini menghasilkan keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) ( \\alpha \\vert 000\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle)\n"
"= \\alpha \\vert 000\\rangle - \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) ( \\alpha \\vert 000\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle)\n"
"= \\alpha \\vert 000\\rangle - \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is exactly the state we would have obtained from encoding the qubit state $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle - \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Indeed, a phase-flip error on any one of the three qubits of the encoding has this same effect, which is equivalent to a phase-flip error occurring on the original qubit prior to encoding.\n"
"Under the assumption that the original quantum state is an unknown state, there's therefore no way to detect that an error has occurred, because the resulting state is a perfectly valid encoding of a different qubit state.\n"
"In particular, running the error detection circuit from before on the state $\\alpha \\vert 000\\rangle - \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle$ is certain to result in the syndrome $00,$ which wrongly suggests that no errors have occurred.\n"
msgstr ""
"yang merupakan tepat keadaan yang kita akan peroleh daripada pengekodan keadaan qubit $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle - \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Memang, ralat phase-flip pada mana-mana satu daripada tiga qubit pengekodan mempunyai kesan yang sama, iaitu setara dengan ralat phase-flip yang berlaku pada qubit asal sebelum pengekodan.\n"
"Dengan andaian bahawa keadaan kuantum asal adalah keadaan yang tidak diketahui, oleh itu tiada cara untuk mengesan bahawa ralat telah berlaku, kerana keadaan yang terhasil adalah pengekodan yang sah sempurna bagi keadaan qubit yang berbeza.\n"
"Khususnya, menjalankan Circuit pengesanan ralat dari sebelumnya pada keadaan $\\alpha \\vert 000\\rangle - \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle$ pasti akan menghasilkan sindrom $00,$ yang secara salahnya mencadangkan tiada ralat berlaku.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Meanwhile, there are now three qubits rather than one that could potentially experience phase-flip errors.\n"
"So, in a situation in which phase-flip errors are assumed to occur independently on each qubit with some nonzero probability $p$ (similar to a binary symmetric channel except for phase-flips rather than bit-flips), this code actually increases the likelihood of a phase-flip error after decoding for small values of $p.$\n"
"To be more precise, we'll get a phase-flip error on the original qubit after decoding whenever there are an odd number of phase-flip errors on the three qubits of the encoding, which happens with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"Sementara itu, kini terdapat tiga qubit dan bukannya satu yang berpotensi mengalami ralat phase-flip.\n"
"Jadi, dalam situasi di mana ralat phase-flip diasumsikan berlaku secara bebas pada setiap qubit dengan kebarangkalian bukan sifar $p$ (serupa dengan saluran simetri binari kecuali untuk phase-flip dan bukannya bit-flip), kod ini sebenarnya meningkatkan kemungkinan ralat phase-flip selepas penyahkodan untuk nilai $p$ yang kecil.\n"
"Lebih tepat lagi, kita akan mendapat ralat phase-flip pada qubit asal selepas penyahkodan bila-bila masa terdapat bilangan ganjil ralat phase-flip pada tiga qubit pengekodan, yang berlaku dengan kebarangkalian\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"3 p (1 - p)^2 + p^3.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"3 p (1 - p)^2 + p^3.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This value is larger than $p$ when $0<p<1/2,$ so the code increases the "
"probability of a phase-flip error for values of $p$ in this range.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilai ini lebih besar daripada $p$ apabila $0<p<1/2,$ jadi kod itu "
"meningkatkan kebarangkalian ralat phase-flip untuk nilai $p$ dalam julat "
"ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Modified repetition code for phase-flip errors {#modified-repetition-code-"
"for-phase-flip-errors}"
msgstr ""
"Kod ulangan yang diubahsuai untuk ralat phase-flip {#modified-repetition-"
"code-for-phase-flip-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've observed that the 3-bit repetition code is completely oblivious to phase-flip errors, so it doesn't seem to be very helpful for dealing with this sort of error.\n"
"We can, however, modify the 3-bit repetition code in a simple way so that it does detect phase-flip errors.\n"
"This modification will render the code oblivious to bit-flip errors — but, as we'll see in the next section, we can combine together the 3-bit repetition code with this modified version to obtain the Shor code, which can correct both bit-flip and phase-flip errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita telah memerhatikan bahawa kod ulangan 3-bit sama sekali tidak menyedari ralat phase-flip, jadi nampaknya tidak begitu membantu untuk menangani jenis ralat ini.\n"
"Namun, kita boleh mengubahsuai kod ulangan 3-bit dengan cara yang mudah supaya ia mengesan ralat phase-flip.\n"
"Pengubahsuaian ini akan menjadikan kod tidak menyedari ralat bit-flip — tetapi, seperti yang akan kita lihat dalam bahagian seterusnya, kita boleh menggabungkan kod ulangan 3-bit dengan versi yang diubahsuai ini untuk mendapatkan kod Shor, yang boleh membetulkan kedua-dua ralat bit-flip dan phase-flip.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is the modified version of the encoding circuit from above, which will now be able to detect phase-flip errors.\n"
"The modification is very simple: we simply apply a Hadamard gate to each qubit after performing the two controlled-NOT gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah versi yang diubahsuai daripada Circuit pengekodan dari atas, yang kini akan dapat mengesan ralat phase-flip.\n"
"Pengubahsuaiannya sangat mudah: kita hanya menggunakan gate Hadamard pada setiap qubit selepas melakukan dua gate controlled-NOT.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Modified encoding circuit for the 3-bit repetition "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-encoder-modified.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit pengekodan yang diubahsuai untuk kod ulangan "
"3-bit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/repetition-encoder-modified.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Hadamard gate transforms a $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state into a $\\vert + "
"\\rangle$ state, and a $\\vert 1\\rangle$ state into a $\\vert - \\rangle$ "
"state, so the net effect is that the single qubit state $\\alpha\\vert "
"0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle$ is encoded as\n"
msgstr ""
"Gate Hadamard mengubah keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle$ kepada keadaan $\\vert + "
"\\rangle$, dan keadaan $\\vert 1\\rangle$ kepada keadaan $\\vert - "
"\\rangle$, jadi kesan keseluruhannya ialah keadaan qubit tunggal "
"$\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle$ dikodkan sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert {+}\\,{+}\\,{+} \\rangle + \\beta \\vert {-}\\,{-}\\,{-} \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert {+}\\,{+}\\,{+} \\rangle + \\beta \\vert {-}\\,{-}\\,{-} \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\vert {+}\\,{+}\\,{+} \\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes\\vert + \\rangle$ and\n"
"$\\vert {-}\\,{-}\\,{-} \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes\\vert - \\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $\\vert {+}\\,{+}\\,{+} \\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes\\vert + \\rangle$ dan\n"
"$\\vert {-}\\,{-}\\,{-} \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes\\vert - \\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A phase-flip error, or equivalently a $Z$ gate, flips between the states $\\vert + \\rangle$ and $\\vert - \\rangle,$ so this encoding will be useful for detecting (and correcting) phase-flip errors.\n"
"Specifically, the error-detection circuit from earlier can be modified as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ralat phase-flip, atau secara setara gate $Z$, membalikkan antara keadaan $\\vert + \\rangle$ dan $\\vert - \\rangle$, jadi pengekodan ini akan berguna untuk mengesan (dan membetulkan) ralat phase-flip.\n"
"Khususnya, Circuit pengesanan ralat dari sebelumnya boleh diubahsuai seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Phase error detection circuit for the 3-bit repetition "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/three-bit-modified-error-detect.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit pengesanan ralat fasa untuk kod ulangan "
"3-bit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/three-bit-modified-error-detect.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In words, we take the circuit from before and simply put Hadamard gates on the top three qubits at both the beginning and the end.\n"
"The idea is that the first three Hadamard gates transform $\\vert + \\rangle$ and $\\vert - \\rangle$ states back into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$ states, the same parity checks as before take place, and then the second layer of Hadamard gates transforms the state back to $\\vert + \\rangle$ and $\\vert - \\rangle$ states so that we recover our encoding.\n"
"For future reference, let's observe that this phase-flip detection circuit can be simplified as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan kata lain, kita mengambil Circuit dari sebelumnya dan hanya meletakkan gate Hadamard pada tiga qubit atas di bahagian awal dan akhir.\n"
"Ideanya ialah tiga gate Hadamard pertama mengubah keadaan $\\vert + \\rangle$ dan $\\vert - \\rangle$ kembali kepada keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert 1\\rangle$, semakan pariti yang sama seperti sebelumnya berlaku, dan kemudian lapisan kedua gate Hadamard mengubah keadaan kembali kepada keadaan $\\vert + \\rangle$ dan $\\vert - \\rangle$ supaya kita memulihkan pengekodan kita.\n"
"Untuk rujukan masa hadapan, marilah kita perhatikan bahawa Circuit pengesanan phase-flip ini boleh dipermudahkan seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Simplified phase error detection "
"circuit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/simplified-phase-error-detect.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit pengesanan ralat fasa yang "
"dipermudahkan](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/simplified-phase-error-detect.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following four circuit diagrams describe how our modified version of the 3-bit repetition code, including the encoding step and the error detection step, functions when at most one phase-flip error occurs.\n"
"The behavior is similar to the ordinary 3-bit repetition code for bit-flips.\n"
msgstr ""
"Empat gambar rajah Circuit berikut menerangkan bagaimana versi yang diubahsuai kod ulangan 3-bit kita, termasuk langkah pengekodan dan langkah pengesanan ralat, berfungsi apabila paling banyak satu ralat phase-flip berlaku.\n"
"Tingkah lakunya serupa dengan kod ulangan 3-bit biasa untuk bit-flip.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Phase-flip error detection for modified 3-bit repetition code (no "
"errors)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/phase-error-none.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pengesanan ralat phase-flip untuk kod ulangan 3-bit yang diubahsuai (tiada"
" ralat)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/phase-error-none.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Phase-flip error detection for modified 3-bit repetition code (error on "
"qubit 0)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/phase-error-0.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pengesanan ralat phase-flip untuk kod ulangan 3-bit yang diubahsuai (ralat"
" pada qubit 0)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/phase-error-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Phase-flip error detection for modified 3-bit repetition code (error on "
"qubit 1)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/phase-error-1.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pengesanan ralat phase-flip untuk kod ulangan 3-bit yang diubahsuai (ralat"
" pada qubit 1)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/phase-error-1.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Phase-flip error detection for modified 3-bit repetition code (error on "
"qubit 2)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/phase-error-2.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pengesanan ralat phase-flip untuk kod ulangan 3-bit yang diubahsuai (ralat"
" pada qubit 2)](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/phase-error-2.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's an analogous table to the one from above, this time considering the "
"possibility of at most one phase-flip error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah jadual yang serupa dengan yang di atas, kali ini "
"mempertimbangkan kemungkinan paling banyak satu ralat phase-flip.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| State | Syndrome | Correction |\n"
"|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert {+}\\,{+}\\,{+} \\rangle + \\beta \\vert {-}\\,{-}\\,{-}\\rangle$ | $00$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert {+}\\,{+}\\,{-}\\rangle + \\beta \\vert {-}\\,{-}\\,{+}\\rangle$ | $01$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert {+}\\,{-}\\,{+}\\rangle + \\beta \\vert {-}\\,{+}\\,{-}\\rangle$ | $11$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert {-}\\,{+}\\,{+} \\rangle + \\beta \\vert {+}\\,{-}\\,{-}\\rangle$ | $10$ | $Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Keadaan | Sindrom | Pembetulan |\n"
"|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert {+}\\,{+}\\,{+} \\rangle + \\beta \\vert {-}\\,{-}\\,{-}\\rangle$ | $00$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert {+}\\,{+}\\,{-}\\rangle + \\beta \\vert {-}\\,{-}\\,{+}\\rangle$ | $01$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert {+}\\,{-}\\,{+}\\rangle + \\beta \\vert {-}\\,{+}\\,{-}\\rangle$ | $11$ | $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"
"| $\\alpha\\vert {-}\\,{+}\\,{+} \\rangle + \\beta \\vert {+}\\,{-}\\,{-}\\rangle$ | $10$ | $Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}$ |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, this modified version of the 3-bit repetition code can now no longer correct bit-flip errors.\n"
"All is not lost, however.\n"
"As suggested previously, we'll be able to combine the two codes we've just seen into one code — the 9-qubit Shor code — that can correct both bit-flip and phase-flip errors, and indeed any error on a single qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Malangnya, versi yang diubahsuai kod ulangan 3-bit ini kini tidak lagi boleh membetulkan ralat bit-flip.\n"
"Namun, tidak semua harapan hilang.\n"
"Seperti yang dicadangkan sebelumnya, kita akan dapat menggabungkan dua kod yang baru kita lihat menjadi satu kod — kod Shor 9-Qubit — yang boleh membetulkan kedua-dua ralat bit-flip dan phase-flip, malah sebarang ralat pada satu qubit.\n"
